  data:  # 3ad8
    kind: work_item  # 3ad8
    title: "smart-test selection test-bed: a small repo with one of each selection scenario, scripted edits and a mutation oracle, so WI-zajuv / WI-gapos iterate in seconds instead of against hypergumbo's ~30k tests"  # 3ad8
    status: todo_soft  # 3ad8
    priority: 3  # 3ad8
    parent:  # 3ad8
    tags:  # 3ad8
    - smart_test  # 3ad8
    - ci_infrastructure  # 3ad8
    isbefore:  # 3ad8
    - WI-zajuv-hisam-pisis-nufom-kudom-mavis-kulud-vokab  # 3ad8
    - WI-gapos-nubuz-vokod-jajul-magid-zajis-nakud-lomit  # 3ad8
    duplicate_of: []  # 3ad8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 3ad8
    pr_ref:  # 3ad8
    description: "Iterating WI-zajuv (text-reader set, comment-only manifest) and WI-gapos (block-level --narrow) against hypergumbo itself is slow and noisy: ~30k tests, a comment-only change selects 814 test files (~17 min), and the 3.4 GB selection index (WI-romam) has history no test controls. Build a small test-bed repo where every selection scenario is present once, a full run takes seconds, and the expected selection for each scenario is written down.\n\nLAYOUT CONSTRAINT (first design question). smart-test takes REPO_ROOT from its own location (`scripts/..`, line 45) and hard-codes the hypergumbo layout: 21 `packages/...` references, including the `--cov=packages/hypergumbo-*/src` list (~line 338); coverage-select imports hypergumbo_core from a path relative to itself; the slice uses the installed stable hypergumbo. Either the test-bed mimics the layout (packages/<pkg>/src/<pkg>/, packages/<pkg>/tests/, root tests/) and a harness copies the current scripts into it, or smart-test reads its layout (source roots, cov roots, test roots) from a small config with today's values as the default. Prefer the second if it is small; it is also what lets the harness test the scripts under change rather than a copy.\n\nSCENARIOS the source must contain (one each, small):\n- a transitive chain A -> B -> C, with a test that reaches C only through A;\n- a runtime dependency with no import (a registry / getattr / string dispatch), so coverage sees what the import graph cannot (WI-kuliv's `explain` example);\n- module-level import-time code, a class with methods, a nested function;\n- a function under `# pragma: no cover`, a `# type:` comment, a docstring read at runtime via `__doc__`;\n- two modules sharing a function name (block qualified-name collisions);\n- tests that read source as TEXT: a comment-marker gate (like the `# axis:` gate), a `file.py:LINE` citation test (WI-lujon), a docstring check, and one whole-tree gate.\n\nEDITS, each a patch with its expected selection: comment-only; docstring-only; one-line body edit in C; signature edit; rename / move of a function; new function; shadowing second `def f`; module-level statement edit; `# pragma` edit; `# type:` edit; deleted module still imported by a test; test-file-only edit; fixture-only edit (INV-kinin's shape).\n\nORACLE. Per edit, the MUST-select set: for code edits, mutate the changed block to raise and run the full test-bed suite; the tests that fail are the floor (a sound lower bound). For text edits, the written list of text-readers. The SHOULD-NOT-select set is written down by hand. Each selector (import slice, union, narrow, WI-zajuv, WI-gapos) is scored against both, so a change is judged by \"dropped a must-select test\" (never acceptable) and \"selected N extra\" (cost).\n\nDone when: the test-bed and harness exist, `harness run <selector>` prints the must/extra table for every edit in seconds, and today's import-graph slice and --narrow are scored as the baseline WI-zajuv and WI-gapos must beat without dropping a must-select test."  # 3ad8
    fields: {}  # 3ad8
